WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.870
Think you know a lot about music?

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:05.230
Here's 23 random music facts that'll blow your mind.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:08.590
Aerosmith's "I Don't Wanna Miss a Thing" was originally written

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:09.710
for Celine Dion.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:10.830
Madonna's "Like a Virgin"

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.070
is actually about a guy getting over a breakup.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.370
Sorry, Mr. Brown,

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.990
"Summer of '69" is about the sexual position.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.390
Sarah McLachlan's "Angel"

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:19.790
 is about heroin addiction.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.280
Semisonic's "Closing Time"

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.590
is not about last call,

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.640
but rather the birth the lead singer's daughter.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.320
The Goo Goo Dolls' "Slide"

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.070
is about abortion.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.680
"A Boy Named Sue" was not written by Johnny Cash,

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:30.990
but rather Shel Silverstein.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.280
Shel wrote, "A Boy Named Sue," among other things.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.400
"Gettin' Jiggy Wit It"

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.520
was written by Nas.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.950
"Nothing Compares to You" and "Manic Monday"

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.280
were both written by Prince.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:42.840
Cee Lo's "Forget You"

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.240
was written by Bruno Mars

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:46.670
And Justin Timberlake's "Rock Your Body" was written by Pharrell

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:48.910
for Michael Jackson's final album.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.590
Alanis Morissette's "You Oughta Know"

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:53.200
is supposedly about Full House's Dave Coulier.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.930
Gwen Stefani's "Hollaback Girl" is a response to Courtney Love's slam of Gwen

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:58.240
in Seventeen magazine.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.550
Okay, now pay attention.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.160
Britney's "Toxic" was originally written for Kylie Minogue.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.150
and "I'm a Slave 4 U" was originally written for Janet Jackson.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:07.570
TLC passed on "Baby One More Time,"

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:10.190
while Britney herself passed on Lady Gaga's "Telephone"

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:11.310
and Rihanna's "Umbrella."

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:13.550
Meanwhile Rihanna passed on Miley's "We Can't Stop,

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:15.970
but recorded "Disturbia" instead of Chris Brown.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:16.720
Did you get all that?

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.150
P!nk and Hilary Duff both turned down Kelly Clarkson's

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:20.270
"Since U Been Gone."

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:24.000
Shania Twain and Faith Hill both turndown Beyonce's "Irreplaceable."

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:27.170
Michael Jackson's "Bad" was originally supposed to be a duet with Prince.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.910
And finally, "Lucy in the Sky with Diamonds" is not about LSD.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.080
This is the truth: my son came home with a drawing

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:37.630
and showed me this strange-looking woman flying around.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.660
I said, "What is it?" He said "It's Lucy in the Sky with Diamonds."

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:41.920
And I thought, "That's beautiful."

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.790
I immediately wrote a song about it.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:45.650
 Check the description for sources

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.640
and let us know your favorite music fact.

